The original BallZ control model as scene vocabulary, per BALLZ_GAME_DESIGN
(layouts faithful; control/camera/feel adapted from the author's design):

- steering block on dynamic entities, integrated in the deterministic step:
  heading, thrust/turn inputs, per-direction speed cap (brake and turn keep
  authority at the cap), kick impulse, runtime-anchored fire-arrow (arrowId)
- api.steer on BOTH implementations + bridge manifest (control.steer);
  inputs land on edges, serialisation carries pose+tuning, never inputs
- caged ball: the wireframe cage IS the physics sphere, checkered core
  parented inside; mass 1.7 / friction .55 / restitution .5
- play layer: keyboard aim/thrust/brake/kick + mouse point-to-aim and
  click / drag-for-power, chosen by the scene (steering block present);
  composed courses keep the per-axis push scheme
- chase camera in the one shared tick at ~38°, yaw follows the arrow,
  replaces controls.update() for the frame; orbit target stays synced
- classic levels honour levelList.xml nbrTour=3; laps-reduced-to-one retired
- smoke-ballz: steering/arrow/cap/brake/kick/chase/laps assertions; waits
  keyed to the HUD's own repaint and the runtime's phase, not wall-clock
